    "updated_at": "2026-09-29T09:08:07Z",
    "body": "On task vs. microtask, I tweaked @domenic's test case to check in a volumechange event, which is fired from a task on the same task source:\r\nhttps://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=14894\r\n\r\nChrome, Firefox and Safari all agree that `paused` is false in the queued microtask, but true when the volumechange event fires.\r\n\r\nEven though a microtask would make sense here, I don't think we should bother changing this when implementations agree on using a task.",
